	"web_text": "For the Kuba, a ranked society, an ostentatious show of wealth indicates an individual's status and fuels an array of elaborate costuming for everyday and ceremonial wear among titleholders. Hats covered with a combination of beads, cowrie shells, and feathers are the privilege of the high-ranking titleholders, whose status is announced by the formal deviation from a simple cap to a taller, conical hat and the use of embellishment.",
